# Did anybody look for couplings between this stack's layers? One row per filing that was asked,
# carrying what it answered and the note that argues for the answer.
#
# Independent layers, or nobody who looked
#   A stack with no couplings filed has either independent layers or nobody who looked, and an
#   empty coupling table renders those two identically. They are opposite claims: one licenses
#   treating each remainder on its own, the other says nothing at all. This is where the difference
#   lives.
#
# A null `answer` is not an absence
#   It means the document filed real couplings, so the search question is answered by the content
#   rather than by a reason.
#
# Its own file, so the union can be taken half at a time
#   epistemics/searches.sqlc unions this with the elimination search. Built inline as one relation
#   with a `looked_for` string, every caller wanting one kind of search has to filter on that
#   string, and callers give up and read pm.coupling_search raw. entries/coupling_presence.sqlc and
#   reports/independence_tested.sqlc compose this half directly. A union whose members were never
#   files is a union nobody can compose half of.
-- pm:Stack/pm:couplings/pm:absent, one row per filing asked.
SELECT cs.filing, cs.absent AS answer, cs.note
FROM pm.coupling_search cs
